      <rules>
        <rule id="d33c-7b7b-1b38-ab17" name="Suppression Protocols" hidden="false">
          <description>In your Shooting phase, after this model has shot, select one enemy unit (excluding **^^Monsters^^** and **^^Vehicles^^**) hit by one or more of those attacks made with an Armiger autocannon. Until the start of your next turn, that enemy unit is suppressed. While that unit is suppressed, each time a model in that unit makes an attack, subtract 1 from the Hit roll.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="8c25-39f9-ffd5-5d34" name="Deadly Demise" hidden="false">
          <description>Some models have 'Deadly Demise x' listed in their abilities. When such a model is destroyed, roll one D6 before removing it from play (if such a model is a TRANSPORT, roll before any embarked models disembark). On a 6, each unit within 6" of that model suffers a number of mortal wounds denoted by 'x' (if this is a random number, roll separately for each unit within 6").</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="32cc-0fe5-a1b9-2b42" name="Damaged: 1-5 Wounds Remaining" hidden="false">
          <description>While this model has 1-5 wounds remaining, subtract 3 from this model's Objective Control characteristic and each time this model makes an attack, subtract 1 from the Hit roll.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="9f19-9873-ffa1-19ba" name="Invulnerable Save (5+*)" hidden="false">
          <description/>
        </rule>
      </rules>
